  "notes": "FILED ON BOTH TRIGGERS. Composite delta is -6.6 (above the 5.0 magnitude trigger) AND the assessed band (Critical) differs from the published band (Developing), so the band-crossing clause applies independently. PLACEHOLDER CORRECTION, NOT A DECLINE FINDING: Kazakhstan has never been individually assessed (last_assessed: null); its published 20.3 is a seed value shared byte-for-byte with eleven other countries (Algeria, Cameroon, Djibouti, Gabon, Guinea, Honduras, Mauritania, Papua New Guinea, Republic of Congo, Uzbekistan, Zimbabwe). Three cluster members have already been de-seeded: Djibouti and Mauritania to 17.5 and Zimbabwe to 10.0, all on 2026-08-16, all crossing Developing to Critical. Kazakhstan at 13.7 sits between Zimbabwe (10.0) and Djibouti/Mauritania (17.5), and above regional peers Azerbaijan (9.4) and Tajikistan (7.8), which is where an upper-middle-income state with a functioning if exclusionary social safety net and severe civic repression should sit. RECOMMEND EXTENDING THE DE-SEEDING PROGRAMME to the remaining eight cluster members: Algeria, Cameroon, Gabon, Guinea, Honduras, Papua New Guinea, Republic of Congo and Uzbekistan. The 23 August 2026 election is a scheduled future event and was NOT scored.",
